<!-- False positives in the OWASP Dependency-Check scan (the plugin in pom.xml).

     A suppression is only for a CVE that does not apply to the artifact it was
     matched to: one filed against another product with a similar name, or against
     code the application never loads. A real vulnerability is fixed by upgrading
     (CLAUDE.md, "Dependencies and vulnerabilities"), never suppressed. Each
     <suppress> matches one artifact (packageUrl) and one CVE, and its <notes> name
     the CVE, why it does not apply, and when to look at it again. -->
